# Default set vocabulary: words, not numbers.
#
# Copied to <home>/sets.rec on first use; edit that copy and add codes as you
# need them. Each entry has a Code (2-8 capital letters or digits, used in disc
# ids such as TRIP-01_201907_Q) and any number of Parent codes, so the
# vocabulary is a directed acyclic graph (a polyhierarchy, like SKOS
# "broader"): SCAN sits under both RECORDS and PHOTO. Entries without a Parent
# are top-level groups. Order (optional) sorts siblings for display.
#
# A disc has one Set (its id prefix and numbering) and any number of extra
# Category codes; it records every vocabulary path of both (Path fields), so
# the disc stays understandable without this file. Never reuse a code for a
# different meaning: add a new one instead.

%rec: Set
%key: Code
%mandatory: Code Name
%type: Order int

Code: MEMORIES
Name: Memories
Description: personal photos, video and audio
Order: 1

Code: PHOTO
Name: Photos
Description: photographs from cameras and phones
Parent: MEMORIES

Code: TRIP
Name: Trips and holidays
Description: photos and video from travel
Parent: PHOTO

Code: FAMILY
Name: Family
Description: family life, children, relatives
Parent: PHOTO

Code: EVENT
Name: Events
Description: weddings, birthdays, celebrations, gatherings
Parent: PHOTO

Code: VIDEO
Name: Home video
Description: video recordings and home movies
Parent: MEMORIES

Code: AUDIO
Name: Audio recordings
Description: voice memos, recordings, own music
Parent: MEMORIES

Code: RECORDS
Name: Records
Description: documents and paperwork
Order: 2

Code: SCAN
Name: Scans
Description: scanned paper documents and photo prints
Parent: RECORDS
Parent: PHOTO

Code: LETTERS
Name: Letters and correspondence
Description: letters, cards, email printouts
Parent: RECORDS

Code: LEGAL
Name: Legal and identity
Description: contracts, certificates, passports, wills, deeds
Parent: RECORDS

Code: TAXES
Name: Taxes
Description: tax returns and supporting documents
Parent: FINANCE

Code: FINANCE
Name: Finance
Description: bank statements, invoices, insurance, payslips
Parent: RECORDS

Code: HEALTH
Name: Health
Description: medical records, prescriptions, test results
Parent: RECORDS

Code: HOME
Name: Home and property
Description: house, renovations, manuals, warranties
Parent: RECORDS

Code: CAREER
Name: Work and study
Order: 3

Code: WORK
Name: Work
Description: job and career material
Parent: CAREER

Code: SCHOOL
Name: School and study
Description: courses, notes, theses
Parent: CAREER

Code: PROJECTS
Name: Projects
Description: things you made
Order: 4

Code: PROJ
Name: Personal projects
Description: a project's files of every kind together (code, designs, notes, photos)
Parent: PROJECTS

Code: CODE
Name: Software
Description: source code and programming projects
Parent: PROJECTS

Code: ELEC
Name: Electronics
Description: circuits, PCBs, firmware, hardware projects
Parent: PROJECTS

Code: DESIGN
Name: Design and art
Description: drawings, CAD, 3D printing, graphics
Parent: PROJECTS

Code: WRITING
Name: Writing
Description: articles, stories, blogs, books
Parent: PROJECTS

Code: COLLECT
Name: Collections
Description: things you gathered rather than made
Order: 5

Code: BOOKS
Name: Books and papers
Description: e-books, articles, reference material
Parent: COLLECT

Code: MEDIA
Name: Media library
Description: films, music albums, podcasts
Parent: COLLECT

Code: GAMES
Name: Games
Description: games, saves, mods
Parent: COLLECT

Code: BACKUPS
Name: Backups and exports
Order: 6

Code: SYSTEM
Name: System backups
Description: computer backups and disk images
Parent: BACKUPS

Code: PHONE
Name: Phone backups
Description: phone backups and exports
Parent: BACKUPS

Code: EMAIL
Name: Email and messages
Description: mailbox exports, chat exports
Parent: BACKUPS

Code: WEB
Name: Web archives
Description: saved websites (WARC), social media exports
Parent: BACKUPS

Code: MISC
Name: Miscellaneous
Description: material that fits nowhere else yet
Order: 9
